\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Dollar closed Friday at $4,198.7, surpassing its all-time high\b0\par\par\uc2 500 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 This Friday, the dollar closed at $4,198.78 on average, which represented an increase of $47.57 against the Market Representative Rate (MRR), which for today's trading day is at $4,151.21, as the risk of economic recession in the United States increases.The opening price registered by the Set-\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  platform was $4,174.98, while the maximum reached $4,209.99, reaching historical levels, and the minimum $4,174.98. During the day, more than US$1,064 million was traded through 1,444 transactions.One factor that could explain the behavior of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to do with the decision taken on Thursday by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to increase the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate by 150 basis points, bringing it to 7.5% in June.\par \par \uc2  This is configured as the strongest increase in the recent history of the country.Read here: Petro achieves support from all economic sectors to the designation of Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Antonio Ocampo as MinhaciendaThe decision was taken unanimously by the members of the Board of Directors of the Banco de la Rep\u250\'00\'FAblica, a situation that has not been seen in recent decisions, when in fact, other members have voted for even higher increases."We are giving a signal that we are in a process of adjustment, which probably will not be the last, but we will know with the information we have in due course," said Leonardo Villar, manager of the Issuer.Meanwhile, another bout of risk aversion swept through global markets on Friday, sending U.S. stock futures lower and bolstering bonds on an ominous start to the second half of 2022.The 10-year \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yield fell below 3% to the lowest level since early June. All Group of 10 \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell against the dollar and the yen, traditional safe havens.Risk assets continued to be targeted by sellers on Friday as concerns about recession outweighed worries about runaway inflation for now. As Fed policymakers are determined to bring price growth back to their 2% target, investors are assessing the impact on the economy of sharp rate hikesAnother factor behind the dollar's rise is crude oil, which has seen down days over the past week. However, today the price of Brent oil, the reference for Colombia, reaches US$111.53; while the West Texas Intermediate (WTI) is trading at US$ 108.23.Finally, for analysts such as \uc2 Edward Moya\uc2  of Oanda Markets, "the behavior of the dollar obeys a global trend that has its roots in the abrupt movements and volatility of the markets, which change their path according to the news due to the war in Ukraine, the blockades in China and, now, the vacation season in the northern hemisphere, where consumption increases strongly. But, no doubt, volatile market movements can be mitigated by central banks, which continue to choose to raise interest rates to curb the current liquidity."\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220701ei7100e4x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw109\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1635\pichgoal600
