\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 BanRep Fees Decision; Stock exchanges, oil drop: Colombia Today\b0\par\par\uc2 833 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 (Bloomberg) -- U.S. Futures fall and European stock markets are heading for their biggest weekly decline since June as investors weigh the prospects for a new stimulus package in the U.S. with the global uptick in coronavirus cases. Yield 10-year Treasury bonds, Bloomberg Dollar index advances and MSCI index of emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rises after four days of losses. WTI oil decreases to about USD40 to concern about the outlook for consumption amid the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 In Colombia, the Bank of the Republic holds its monetary policy meeting, where 12 out of 22 analysts surveyed by Bloomberg expect the board to cut the interest rate for the seventh consecutive meeting to an all-time low of 1.75% since the current 2%, while the rest expect no change.\par \par \uc2 Avianca Holdings\uc2  advisors said their $2 billion bankruptcy financing package does not depend on a loan offered by the Colombian government, which has been criticized by lawmakers and is currently suspended by a local court.\par \par \uc2 Banco de Bogot\u225\'00\'E1\uc2  made its first placement of green bonds amounting to COP300 billion and where demand amounted to COP913.271 million. Cutting rates were IBR +1.14% at 3 years and fixed rate 4.75% at 5 years.\par \par \uc2 The peso halted its path of losses and appreciated 0.9% closing at 3,827 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, 6,555 new cases of coronavirus were reported and 178 deaths were recorded, according to data from the Ministry of Health. With this, the number of total confirmed cases rose to 790,823 and the deceased reached 24,924.\par \par \uc2 Colombia is the country with the fifth highest number of total cases of contagion, according to data from \uc2 Johns Hopkins University\uc2 , surpassed by the US, India, Brazil and Russia.\par \par \uc2 According to Bloomberg's calculations:\par \par \uc2 Cases +0.8% vs +0.9% moving average 7 daysDeaths +0.7% vs +0.8% moving average 7 daysPositivity tests 18.5% vs 20.0% moving average 7 daysAll events in local time.\par \par \uc2 International:\par \par \uc2 Operators should quell their nervousness by the possibility that a delay in the U.S. election result could disrupt markets, according to \uc2 Goldman Sachs\par \par \uc2 While a delay in the outcome is a "tail risk," initial results along with voter turnout, county-level data, and the high correlation of voting errors in all states suggests investors will have enough information on election night to determine the likely winner, economists Michael Cahill and Alec Phillips wrote in a comment on ThursdaySeveral states, including some decisive ones, allow votes to be processed and counted well before Election Day, notedMexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered its key interest rate by a quarter of a point, the lowest since February, in a sign that the current cycle of monetary easing is coming to an end after inflation exceeded the targetBanxico's board, led by Governor Alejandro D\u237\'00\'EDaz de Leon, voted unanimously to reduce borrowing costs to 4.25%, in line with 18 out of 23 estimates in a Bloomberg survey. Four economists hoped the bank would not lower rates, while one thought it would offer another half-point cut, at the same rate as the previous five decisionsTO BE PENDING:\par \par \uc2 In Colombia:BanRep decision fees; 13 analysts estimate -25pbs at 1.75%, and 9 see unchanged rate at 2%Auctions:Expansion \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  include 9-month repos per COP1 billion, and 31 days per COP1 billionInternational:7:30am: U.S. orders durable goodsAugust P; Est. 1.4%, previous 11.4%Fed Agenda:8am: Williams (New York) talks to community development leaders11:15am: George (Kansas) talks about community banks2:10pm: Williams (New York) talks about the workforce during covid-19Relevant agendas:South americaUs.MexicoBrazilEuropeNews:\par \par \uc2 Traders bet on a last rate cut in ColombiaUS$2,000 \uc2 Avianca\uc2  plan does not depend on Colombia's aidBogota Bank places COP300,000m in 1st sale of green bondsAvianca restarts international flights from Colombia 28 Sept.Highlights of Latin America's top newspapersComment:\par \par \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  expects \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reduce its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate by 25pbs to 1.75%, changing its previous estimate of rate stability"In addition to the surprise of August inflation, labour market weakness remains extremely high, with total employment of 19% in July since its pre-crisis level (i.e., nearly one in five workers has quit or lost their jobs since February," analyst Paulo Mateus writes in a reportGiven that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided to cut interest rates in a unanimous decision in August, that shows that even the most hawkish member of the board saw the need to provide greater monetary stimulus"The IBR swap curve is discounting a higher probability of another cut in the short term, so while a rate cut in September would surprise most analysts surveyed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the market reaction would likely be contained, alleviating concerns that another cut could lead to greater financial volatility and possible tightening of financial conditions"\par \par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A92020 \uc2 Bloomberg L.P\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020200925eg9p004aj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
