\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Surging coronavirus cases roil Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , economic fears mount\b0\par\par\uc2 606 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2020\par 20:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Brazilian real slides to new record low\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazil \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  thrice in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market  \par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Colombia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peso tracks declines in oil prices\par \par  (Adds comments, updates prices)\par     By Shreyashi Sanyal\par     March 5 (Reuters) - Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tumbled on\par Thursday, with Brazil's real touching new lows, as the rapid\par spread of the coronavirus outside China pushed investors away\par from riskier assets on growing worries about the scale of the\par economic damage.  \par     Brazil's real continued its slide, falling 1.4% to a\par fresh low of 4.6663 to the dollar, while Mexico's peso\par lost more than 1.7% heading for its third straight session of\par losses.\par     "The market is getting more concerned about the impact to\par growth globally and what you are seeing is that a slowdown in\par global growth creates concerns for growth in emerging market\par economies," said Jeff Grills, head of emerging markets debt at\par Aegon Asset Management. \par     "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakness is one way you can see that slowdown\par being expressed."\par     Colombia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slid nearly 2%, tracking losses\par in oil prices, while Chile's peso touched a three-month\par low despite a rise in its main export good, copper.\par   \par     The weakness in regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was in line with broader\par emerging market peers and came even as the dollar languishes at\par two-month lows as investors bet the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  will\par reduce lending rates further after delivering an emergency\par interest rate cut on Tuesday. \par     Hopes have risen that other central banks might follow suit\par as the virus spreads aggressively across the globe, forcing\par whole cities to shut down and bringing economic activity in\par those areas to a standstill.\par     The number of infected cases globally is fast approaching\par 100,000, and the death toll has climbed to over 3,300. \par     In Brazil, the deteriorating economic outlook for 2020\par exacerbated in recent days by coronavirus fears, raised bets the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will cut interest rates for the sixth time since\par the beginning of its easing cycle in 2019, at its March 17-18\par meeting to a new low of 4%.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Brazil\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  derivatives\par market three times on Thursday, selling a total of $3 billion\par swaps contracts, but the pressure is mounting on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to tap its $360 billion stockpile of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves and sell\par dollars outright to ease the pressure on the real.\par     "They (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazil \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) will eventually get to a point\par where if it approaches 5 reais to the dollar, that is where they\par can get a lot more success. That is when people will realize\par that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has moved too far relative to general\par expectations for fair value," Grills said. \par     Sao Paulo stocks shed almost 4%, led lower by\par carriers Gol and Azul because airlines\par have been one of the worst hit by the outbreak as travel curbs\par restrict demand.       \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1937 GMT:\par    \par   Stock indexes                Latest        Daily % change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets              1037.54           -0.03\par                                              \par  MSCI LatAm                         2383.61           -4.94\par                                              \par  Brazil Bovespa                   103011.63           -3.93\par                                              \par  Mexico IPC                        42518.26           -2.04\par                                              \par  Chile IPSA                         4324.09           -0.97\par                                              \par  Argentina MerVal                  36771.53          -1.267\par                                              \par  Colombia COLCAP                    1543.79           -0.05\par                                              \par                                                            \par       \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest        Daily % change\par  Brazil real                         4.6459           -1.43\par                                              \par  Mexico peso                        19.8910           -1.82\par                                              \par  Chile peso                           823.2           -0.80\par                                              \par  Colombia peso                         3537           -1.75\par                                              \par 