\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED-EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  up on dovish Yellen; Colombia peso jumps\b0\par\par\uc2 493 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2016\par 01:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Corrects in fifth paragraph to say oil prices hit 8-month\par highs)\par     By Bruno Federowski\par     SAO PAULO, June 7 (Reuters) - Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strengthened on Tuesday after U.S. Federal Reserve Chair Janet\par Yellen refrained from setting a time frame for further interest\par rate hikes.\par     In a speech on Monday, Yellen did not repeat her assessment\par that rate increases would be appropriate in coming months.\par Nevertheless, she gave a largely upbeat assessment of the U.S.\par economy and indicated further hikes were coming. \par     Emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tend to benefit from low interest\par rates abroad, which often drive foreign investors toward\par high-yielding bonds.\par     The Colombian peso shot up more than 2 percent, its\par biggest daily gain since mid-April, and far outperformed its\par peers.\par     A rally in oil prices  to eight-month highs\par also boosted the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after a spate of attacks on\par infrastructure in Nigeria depressed crude supply.\par     The peso had been pressured after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Colombia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par backed off its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy. However, bets that the bank\par could increase rates to fight \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakness grew following a\par report showing inflation kept rising well above its long-term\par target. \par     The Brazilian real strengthened 0.5 percent after\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief nominee Ilan Goldfajn defended the country's\par floating exchange rate in a Senate hearing. \par     "The market interpreted that as a sign that there will be\par less meddling in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market when Ilan\par (Goldfajn) takes charge," said Spinelli brokerage trader Jos\u233\'00\'E9\par Carlos Amado.\par     Many traders took the words as a sign that Goldfajn would\par allow the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to strengthen past 3.50 per U.S. dollar, a\par milestone that often triggered \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  under the current\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief.\par     The real had weakened by as much as 0.7 percent in morning\par trading following local news reports that Brazil's top\par prosecutor had demanded the arrest of several high-ranking\par politicians. \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1450 GMT:\par  Stock indexes                               daily %    YTD %\par                                               change   change\par                                    Latest             \par  MSCI Emerging Markets               837.19     1.69     3.67\par  MSCI LatAm                         2142.55     1.19    15.71\par  Brazil Bovespa                    50628.78     0.39    16.79\par  Mexico IPC                        46230.43     0.81     7.57\par  Chile IPSA                         4009.65     0.55     8.95\par  Chile IGPA                        19729.34     0.49     8.69\par  Argentina MerVal                  13106.86     1.98    12.26\par  Colombia IGBC                      9769.51     