\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  peso weakens after cenbank backs off  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2016\par 23:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Updates prices)\par     By Bruno Federowski\par     SAO PAULO, May 31 (Reuters) - The Colombian peso weakened on\par Tuesday after the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announced it would\par suspend an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy aimed at slowing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par decline.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Friday it would not hold any\par additional dollar option sales, but it did not fully rule out\par further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     The bank also increased its benchmark interest rate for a\par ninth consecutive month on Friday, to 7.25 percent, confirming\par the expectations of most analysts in a Reuters poll and pushing\par the peso down 0.75 percent to 3,091 per dollar. \par     The Colombian peso has weakened more than 8 percent\par so far this month to its lowest since early April. Expectations\par of higher U.S. interest rates and a decline in the price of oil,\par a key export and source of tax revenue, weighed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "This announcement eliminates a source of risk when taking\par on USD/COP positions and should therefore expedite the COP\par depreciation path," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nomura Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  strategist Mario Castro\par wrote in a client note.\par     Colombian markets were closed on Monday due to a local\par holiday.\par     The Brazilian real also weakened on Tuesday after the\par release of leaked recordings resulted in a minister quitting\par interim President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Michel Temer\f28 \uc2 \f2 's administration, the second such\par departure since he took over from leftist \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dilma Rousseff\f28 \uc2 \f2  this\par month. \par     Investors worry political instability could weaken the\par government's ability to gain lawmaker support for austerity\par measures as Latin America's biggest economy battles a deep\par recession and stubbornly high inflation.\par     Brazil's benchmark Bovespa stock index also fell\par more than 1 percent.\par \par  (Reporting by Bruno Federowski; editing by Dan Grebler and\par Cynthia Osterman)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-5-31T22:01:28.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160531ec5v01qku\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
