\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  Questioned as Peso Slides -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,312 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2014\par 14:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 8:58 EDT - Some economists are asking why \uc2 Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to buy dollars to weaken the peso when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already fallen 7% in seven weeks, to 1981/USD? "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should soon reassess their \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy," Jefferies says in a research note. Bank officials have their reasons; an even weaker peso would further help Colombian exporters, and keeping up with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will build \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves against shocks. But Jefferies says "this strategy could be self-defeating if it feeds into a vicious cycle of de-leveraging and then need for more USD as well as the pressure on the inflation target." (dan.molinski@wsj.com @dmwsj)\par \par \uc2 8:38 EDT - Bond prices hit fresh session lows after mixed retail sales. The headline number showed 0.6% growth, a tad below 0.7% forecast by economists, though excluding automotive purchases, sales rose 0.3% from July, vs 0.2% forecast. The key focus is the FOMC meeting next week and any changes in the \uc2 Fed\uc2 's language regarding how long it will hold rates near zero could send bond yields higher still. The 10-year Treasury note was 15/32 lower, yielding 2.589%. (min.zeng@wsj.com; @minzengwsj)\par \par \uc2 1237 GMT The Spanish Treasury launches a long overdue three-year government bond at its next auction on Sept. 18, with maturity in October 2017 and a coupon, or annual fixed interest, of 0.50%. Analysts have been eyeing this bond for a while, given the relatively high outstanding volume of the previous three-year bond, the 2.10% April 2017. National treasuries and debt agencies launch new bonds in different sectors of the yield curve on a regular basis, which helps them keep their redemption profile smooth in order to avoid distortions in terms of pricing and future refinancing needs. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 8:26 EDT - After a brief pause Thursday, Treasurys pull back again, with the 10-year yield trading at highest level in more than a month. Worries over next week's FOMC, higher yields in euro zone and new debt supply have sparked selling in Treasurys this week, a setback from the roaring market in 2014. US retail sales are due at 8:30 a.m. and a strong report likely adds more selling to the market over jitters that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  could raise rates sooner than expected. The 10-year Treasury note was 12/32 lower, yielding 2.578%. (min.zeng@wsj.com; @minzengwsj)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1208 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--The Bank of Russia left interest rates unchanged today, but may still lift key rates by 50 bps before the end of the year, as "inflation is set to rise further over the coming months and upside risks are building," says Capital Economics. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Russia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  noted Friday that geopolitical tension and mutual sanctions are fueling inflation above the previously set cap. (alexander.kolyandr@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 8:07 EDT - Brazil reports a bigger-than-expected increase in economic activity in July, but that won't reverse expectations for a tepid economic performance this year, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco Fator\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's economic activity index, or IBC-Br, picked up 1.5% in July from the previous month on a seasonally adjusted basis, after two consecutive months of declines. For this year, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco Fator\f28 \uc2 \f2  economists expect an expansion of just 0.3% and for 2015 a growth of 0.8%. Consumer and business confidence remain at low levels. (rogerio.jelmayer@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1153 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--\f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  has taken profit on its short AUD/USD trade recommendation. "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pair has hit our target of 0.9050 for a gain of 3.2%," the bank says, while expecting further weakness for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  towards the end of the year. The Australian dollar is now trading around 0.9054. (chiara.albanese@wsj.com @chiaraalbanese) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1151 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Emerging market and central Europe \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue to be affected by the divergent path of monetary policy in U.S. and EU, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Strategists at the bank are particularly bearish HUF and TRY. South Africa is instead a compelling cause for a monetary policy pause. "We expect the SARB's MPC to keep the policy rate unchanged at next week's meeting," Citi says. USD/TRY is now at 2.2021, while EUR/HUF is trading at 314.85. (chiara.albanese@wsj.com @chiaraalbanese) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1144 GMT Analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  revise their year-end GBP/USD forecasts lower as the exchange rate enters "what might be a perfect storm." The bank says while U.S. economic data is surpassing expectations, the U.K. is continuing to disappoint, forcing interest rate expectations lower. Add to the mix the heightened uncertainty about the likely outcome of the Scottish referendum which has added political risk into GBP. \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  revises down its year-end 2014 GBP/USD forecast to 1.60 from 1.68 and the year-end 2015 forecast down to 1.55 from 1.58. GBP/USD currently trades at 1.6230. (nick.cawley@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1123 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--\f28 \uc2 \f2 Denmark's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will auction the 2.50% November 2016 and 1.75% November 2025 bonds next Tuesday, and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Danske\f28 \uc2 \f2  is upbeat on both reopenings. The 2016-dated bond is trading at a negative yield--currently at -0.04%, according to Tradeweb--but given the possibility of a rate cut by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Danish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  [independent from the ECB] because EUR/DKK has dropped "well" below the central parity at 7.4608, the 2016-dated bond is "the best bet," says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Danske\f28 \uc2 \f2 's chief analyst \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jens Peter Sorensen\f28 \uc2 \f2 . For the 2025-dated bond \f28 \uc2 \f2 Danske\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects "solid" demand, given the yield pick-up to Germany, Mr. Sorensen says. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1109 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--After posted the steepest drop in nearly six years in July, Brazil's retail sales are likely to remain in negative territory in the 3Q, says Luciano Rostagno, chief strategist at Banco Mizuho. "Given the continued low levels of consumer confidence in Brazil, it is very likely that retails sales will remain in negative territory in the third quarter, weighing on economic growth," says Mr. Rostagno. Retail sales tumbled 1.1% in July from June. (rogerio.jelmayer@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 7:08 EDT - After a lengthy period of inaction in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, things have become interesting. Traders have decided that even if the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  isn't about to hike rates in a hurry, the direction of U.S. policy is now distinctly closer to "normalization" than that of its major counterparts in Europe and Japan, with far-reaching consequences. A move to six-year lows for the yen has spurred interest in Japanese stocks. Today there are signs that sentiment might be shifting back to the "no" vote on Scottish independence, but the overall message is that even the pound is a riskier bet than the dollar. Thus the recovery of the greenback could well continue for some time, which will have significant impact over time on trade relations and on markets. (michael.casey@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 12, 2014 08:58 ET (12:58 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140912ea9c001nj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
