\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  Not Weakening Peso -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,236 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 2014\par 17:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 11:34 EDT - On Wall Street, an oft-repeated line is "don't fight the Fed," as the US \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pumps money into the economy. \uc2 Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though, apparently doesn't have as much pull in its markets. In late June the bank said it was doubling its official dollar purchases to $2B between July and September to force the peso weaker to help exporters. Board member Mauricio Cardenas declared: "The peso's current exchange rate is not good for the country." Three weeks later, COP not only isn't weaker as \uc2 Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was hoping, it's 1.5% stronger at 1,857/USD as investors bet on continued heavy dollar inflows. (dan.molinski@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 11:32 EDT - Last week's Canada jobs report marked the end of a 6-year run in which the comparable Canadian unemployment rate had been below that of the US. \uc2 Canadian government\uc2  officials have boasted about the country's superior job-creation record after the recession. That message may no longer apply when compared to the US, says TD Bank after looking at metrics such as the participation rate among people 25-54. Labor-market slack had been more significant in the US, but that's now converging. TD adds recent strength in the Canadian dollar versus the greenback "belies the convergence" in the two countries' labor markets. (paul.vieira@wsj.com; @paulvieira)\par \par \uc2 11:28 EDT - Venezuelan officials have been promising measures including an overhaul to their complex \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  system to turn around a moribund economy, but delays are keeping investors guessing over what kind of political clout President Maduro has to pull off painful adjustments. Jefferies says it's looking for clues in the ruling Socialist party's convention later this month, "with pragmatic measures dependent upon a consolidation of support for President Maduro." Bond investors looking for high yields have helped support Venezuelan debt prices, but Jefferies warns further delays in implementing economic measures may force market participants to become skeptical. (kejal.vyas@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1523 GMT There is scope for a negative surprise for the British pound on Tuesday, when the UK will release its latest inflation data. "The UK retail price index contracted by -1.8% in June. Given its close link with CPI, market expectation of a headline inflation rebound to 1.6% in June may be optimistic," says Valentin Marinov at Citi. Meanwhile, investors are starting to focus on risks associated with the Scottish independence referendum on September 18. Citi's view is still that the 'No' vote would prevail and Scotland would remain a part of the UK. But "concerns about the risks for the pound associated with Scottish independence could undermine sterling sentiment in coming weeks," Mr. Marinov said. (chiara.albanese@wsj.com @chiaraalbanese)\par \par \uc2 11:20 EDT - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy has become increasingly controversial, given its length and intensity, Goldman Sach's economist Alberto Ramos says. Heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  started in May 2013 and still taking place despite the now-benign global emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  environment, helping to keep the Brazilian real increasingly overvalued. That, in turn, is "keeping the economy weak and unbalanced," Ramos says. Some economists already say Brazil's GDP may grow less than 1% in 2014. (Luciana.Magalhaes@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 11:10 EDT - When Yellen speaks before lawmakers tomorrow, she will represent the board, not herself. Brian Edmonds, head of interest rates at \uc2 Cantor Fitzgerald\uc2 , says such testimonies have tend to generate some volatility in markets. "There is a risk that Yellen may sound a little bit more hawkish given the complacency in the markets," says Edmonds. "She may try to wake the market up a bit." (min.zeng@wsj.com;@minzengwsj)\par \par \uc2 11:02 EDT - Economists are expecting Peru to post another weak month of growth in May, but \uc2 UBS\uc2  says that actually could be the start of a slow recovery process. "The strength will depend, amongst other factors, on the extent to which business and consumer confidence start to recover," it says. "The recently announced government stimulus measures and Peru's credit upgrade may help in this respect." \uc2 UBS\uc2  is forecasting economic growth of 3.25% in May, compared to 2% in April. (ryan.dube@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1456 GMT Two big signs of cooling inflation in India today: CPI was up 7.3% year-on-year in June, the slowest pace of increase since the index started in 2012 and comfortably below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target of 8% by the end of the year. The less-watched wholesale-price index, also announced today, was up 5.4%, less than expected. Food inflation is still a worry owing to ongoing drought conditions in much of India. Mumbai-based ratings agency Crisil says it still expects retail inflation to hover between 7.5% and 8% in the coming months. (raymond.zhong@wsj.com, Twitter: @zhonggg)\par \par \uc2 10:50 EDT - The haven bond market is having a rough day as riskier assets perk up. Traders say investors are also booking profit before Yellen's testimony Tuesday. The Fed chief has signaled no rush to raising interest rates, but the debate is heating up between Fed hawks and doves on the timing for a rate hike. "The risk is that she sounds more hawkish than the minutes given the strength in the June jobs report that got released after the June policy meeting," says Anthony Cronin, bond trader at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2 . "This could hit the front end of the curve in particular." Ten-year Treasury notes off 6/32, yielding 2.543%. (min.zeng@wsj.com; @minzengwsj)\par \par \uc2 10:46 EDT - Morningstar has added debt from \uc2 Time Warner Cable\uc2  (TWC) to its list of "bonds to avoid." The debt has rallied significantly since February's buyout deal with \uc2 Comcast\uc2  (CMCSA), but the research firm says there's little room for further improvement. Morningstar adds TWC bond prices could tumble if the merger doesn't get regulatory clearance: The rally seen so far has "no weight given to potential adverse regulatory scenarios." (mike.cherney@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1443 GMT \uc2 Banco Espirito Santo\uc2 's bond yields are still rising as investors fret about the bank's exposure to financial problems higher up the Espirito Santo group. BES's subordinated bonds due 2023 are yielding 13.56%, more than two percentage points higher than Friday's close, Tradeweb data show. Analysts at CreditSights last week said BES's direct and indirect exposures could be as much as EUR1.7 billion ($2.3 billion), which could force the bank to raise new capital or seek government support. Five-year CDS on BES widened 41 bps to 444 bps, according to Markit. (ben.edwards@wsj.com @debtnerd)\par \par \uc2 1440 GMT The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's effort later this year to pump cash into the banking system will provide banks with plenty of liquidity, and that prospect will help keep money market rates steady at around current levels in the near future, says \uc2 DZ Bank\uc2  analyst Hendrik Lodde. The ECB plans to offer several rounds of targeted long-term refinancing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , known as TLTROs, starting with two \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September and December, and due in 2018. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 14, 2014 11:34 ET (15:34 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140714ea7e002cd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
