\par\par \b \uc2 *Colombia Peso Gains to 5-Week High of COP1,915/USD\b0\par\par\uc2 369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Dezember 2013\par 16:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 26 Dec 2013 10:22 EDT *Colombia Peso Gains in Correction to Tapering 'Over-Reaction'- Analyst\par \par \uc2 26 Dec 2013 10:59 EDT  Colombia Peso at 5-Week High; Fed Taper Effect Less Than Expected\par \par \uc2 By Dan Molinski\par \par \uc2 BOGOTA--Colombia's peso hit a five-week high Thursday as traders who bet heavily on the dollar in response to the Federal Reserve's decision to reduce its bond-buying program began to scale back their U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings.\par \par \uc2 Early in Bogota, the peso reached COP1,915 to the dollar, its strongest since mid November. In midmorning trading, it was recently at COP1,917.90.\par \par \uc2 "Investors in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moved heavy into dollars and out of pesos in the weeks leading up to, and the days just after the Fed's tapering decision," said Juan David Valencia, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Colombian brokerage Corredores Asociados. "But this is now seen as somewhat of an overreaction. The investors feel they perhaps bought too many dollars."\par \par \uc2 Some traders felt the peso and other emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could fall sharply when the Fed tapered last week, following a slide by Latin American and other emerging market assets when the Fed earlier in the year started talking about cutting its stimulus program.\par \par \uc2 Despite Thursday's bounce in Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mr. Valencia said the overall effect of the Fed's tapering decision could still lead to a generally weaker peso in the early months of next year. He said he expects the peso to slip to around 1,950 to the dollar during that time.\par \par \uc2 The peso is 8% weaker this year after gaining 10% in 2012. \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aggressively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market earlier this year to weaken the peso and help exporters compete better abroad. But since October, it has reduced official dollar-buying by half to about $15 million daily, on the assumption that Fed tapering and other factors such as deterioration in Colombia's trade balance will weaken the peso naturally.\par \par \uc2 Write to Dan Molinski at dan.molinski@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 26, 2013 10:59 ET (15:59 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131226e9cq000wq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
