\par\par \b \uc2 Colombia Stocks Climb; Peso at 2-Month High\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dan Molinski   \par \uc2 162 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 2013\par 22:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA--Colombian stocks rose Friday, fueled by continued gains in U.S. markets, while the peso reached its strongest level against the dollar since mid-August.\par \par \uc2 The Colcap index, a benchmark for the Colombian Stock Exchange, increased 0.36% to end at 1,763.11 points. The index is 4% lower this year.\par \par \uc2 Colombia's peso closed stronger at COP1,881.78 for a dollar, from COP1,886.95 in the previous trading session, according to Set-\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Earlier in the session it hit a two-month intra-day high of COP1,879.50 for a dollar.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market throughout the year with dollar purchases to prevent excessive strength in the peso, but starting this month it cut its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in half to about $15 million.\par \par \uc2 Write to Dan Molinski at dan.molinski@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 -0- [ 11-10-13 2035GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020131011e9ab000m0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
