\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  Peso Falls as  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Extends  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Stocks Rise\b0\par\par\uc2 170 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2013\par 22:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA--\b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso fell to its weakest point in nearly two weeks Friday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  extended a dollar-buying program aimed at weakening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while Colombian stocks rose modestly.\par \par \uc2 The Colcap index, a benchmark for the Colombian Stock Exchange, gained 0.17% to end at 1,768.52 points.\par \par \uc2 Colombia's peso closed weaker at COP1,908.50 for a dollar, from COP1,903.50 in the previous trading session, according to Set-\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's seven-member board, at its monthly policy meeting Friday, decided to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market until at least the end of the year in an effort to weaken the peso and help Colombian exporters. But for the first time this year, the bank set a limit on its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying it will purchase "up to" $1 billion between October and December.\par \par \uc2 -Write to Dan Molinski at dan.molinski@wsj.com [ 27-09-13 2044GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130927e99r000n4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
