\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Colombia's  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  tumbles as investors eye Fed policy\b0\par\par\uc2 By Helen Murphy   \par \uc2 550 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2013\par 17:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds comment, peso close)\par \par \uc2 BOGOTA, June 20 (Reuters) - Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday declined sharply against the U.S. dollar as the greenback benefited from the U.S. Federal Reserve's indications that the U.S. economy is growing strongly enough for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to start reining in its stimulus program.\par \par \uc2 The peso fell 2.3 percent against the dollar, already weakened by ongoing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by the government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Including the drop so far on Thursday, the peso has fallen 9.7 percent against the dollar in 2013. On Wednesday, the peso closed at 1,939 from 1,896, its biggest one-day decline since December 2010.\par \par \uc2 Investors will now be watching for Colombian policymakers to start dismantling their program of dollar purchases. A peso that is too weak makes imports costly and creates inflationary pressure.\par \par \uc2 But even as the peso declined, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $19.8 million on the spot market on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Federal Reserve Chairman \uc2 Ben Bernanke\uc2  said the Fed's policy-setting committee would likely slow the pace of its stimulative bond purchases in 2013 if the U.S. economy continues to grow. Purchases could end by the middle of next year.\par \par \uc2 "Risk premiums have moved higher. The movement will be moderate but the signals from the Fed yesterday ratify that there's a new tendency toward international fixed income and that's impacting the entire domestic market," said Daniel Lozano, head of economic investigation at Bogota-based brokerage Serfinco.\par \par \uc2 Colombia has attracted record foreign direct investment in recent years, as a U.S.-backed offensive against Marxist rebels and paramilitaries made the nation a much safer place to do business. While the investment helped bolster the economy, it also pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "What's important is that Colombian fundamentals are solid," Finance Minister \uc2 Mauricio Cardenas\uc2  told reporters in Bogota. "It's an economy that surely won't be inconvenienced by decisions made in the United States."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FX INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's central has bought millions of dollars daily on the spot market for months to ease gains in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which last year was among the world's strongest, but some board members have raised concerns about the impact of continuing the program for too long.\par \par \uc2 Cesar Vallejo, a board member of \uc2 Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said recently the bank could decide to amend, or even scrap, the program if necessary.\par \par \uc2 At last month's monetary policy meeting, the bank decided to extend the program through September and buy at least $2.5 billion.\par \par \uc2 Cardenas had made weakening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a priority to help manufacturers and exporters, which have struggled for years with a strong peso.\par \par \uc2 The peso has strengthened steadily over the last decade, with a respite in 2008, from about 2,800 pesos per dollar at the end of 2003, prompting heavy lobbying by industrialists.\par \par \uc2 Strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit exporters the most since salaries, pensions and health benefits are paid in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but overseas buyers pay in devalued dollars. (Reporting by Helen Murphy and Nelson Bocanegra; Editing by Bernadette Baum and Steve Orlofsky)\par \par \uc2 COLOMBIA-PESO/ (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130620e96k000xv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
