\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  Peso Hits One-Year Low on Dollar Rally,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dan Molinski   \par \uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2013\par 18:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA--\b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso, which in 2012 was among the world's best-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar, weakened to a 16-month low Wednesday as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw broad gains and Colombian authorities continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to drive the peso even lower.\par \par \uc2 The peso was recently trading at COP1,854.25 for a dollar, 0.4% lower from Tuesday and its weakest intraday level since January 2012.\par \par \uc2 The Colombian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness is derived largely from recent strength in the dollar against a host of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as investors bet the U.S. economy will continue to gain speed even as growth in Europe and elsewhere stalls.\par \par \uc2 Also pushing \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower is persistent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by the country's monetary authorities. The officials want a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  so Colombian exporters can see improved profits when selling their wares abroad.\par \par \uc2 An economic boom in Colombia in recent years attracted record amounts of foreign investment into the South American country, and allowed the peso to gain 10% against the dollar last year. But this caused serious damage to Colombian exporters of everything from coffee to bananas.\par \par \uc2 To counteract that trend in 2013, \uc2 Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buying $30 million daily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Amid this, the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has weakened 5% so far this year, and while the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is scheduled to end May 31, the bank has indicated it may extend it until year-end.\par \par \uc2 "The government is not satisfied [with the 5% decline] and keeps saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should trade at least at COP1,900/USD," said analysts at RBS.\par \par \uc2 Write to Dan Molinski at dan.molinski@dowjones.com [ 22-05-13 1731GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130522e95m000rl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
