\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  Peso Hits Weakest in 3 Months on  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dan Molinski  \par \uc2 274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2013\par 15:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA--\b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso, the strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Latin America against the dollar last year, fell to its weakest level since late November Tuesday on a combination of increased \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a reduction in foreign investment.\par \par \uc2 Early in Bogota, the peso was at COP1,819 for a dollar, 0.3% weaker from Monday's close and 1.2% weaker from Friday. So far in 2013, the peso is nearly 3% weaker, making it one of the weakest in the region.\par \par \uc2 The peso gained 10% last year, significantly hurting Colombian exporters' profits and leading to widespread calls for monetary authorities to do more to force the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weaker. Exporters of products such as coffee, bananas and cut flowers are among Colombia's biggest employers.\par \par \uc2 When the peso began to rise again in the early days of 2013, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  responded by saying that from February through May it is increasing its daily dollar purchases in the spot market by 50% to at least $30 million. The Colombian government's Treasury said it too would be buying dollars to offset the peso's tendency to rise.\par \par \uc2 "What we're seeing, with the peso now weakening, is the result of the rush by authorities in increasing its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Francisco Chaves, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Corredores Asociados in Bogota.\par \par \uc2 He said less foreign investment in Colombia's oil sector compared with 2012's record year is also pushing the peso lower.\par \par \uc2 Write to Dan Molinski at dan.molinski@dowjones.com [ 26-02-13 1515GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130226e92q000r0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
