\par\par \b \uc2 Colombia Stocks Fall in Line With U.S. Stocks; Peso Ends Flat\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dan Molinski   \par \uc2 177 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2013\par 23:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA--Colombian stocks declined Thursday, tracking lower share prices in the U.S., while the peso treaded water against the dollar ahead of a beefed-up \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program by \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Colcap index, a benchmark for the Colombian Stock Exchange, fell 0.20% to end at 1,866.21 points.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended little changed at COP1,7775.27 to the dollar from COP1,776.51 the previous day. On Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will start buying at least $30 million a day in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in an effort to halt the peso's year-long gains versus the dollar. The bank had been buying a daily minimum of $20 million, so the new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  represents a 50% increase.\par \par \uc2 The yield on \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso-denominated bond due in 2020 closed at 4.980%, up from 4.967% a day earlier.\par \par \uc2 Write to Dan Molinski at dan.molinski@dowjones.com [ 31-01-13 2204GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130131e91v001e6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
