\par\par \b \uc2 Colombian Peso Strengthens After ECB Keeps Rates on Hold\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dan Molinski   \par \uc2 157 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2013\par 15:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA--Colombia's peso is at its strongest level in a week Thursday morning due to broad weakness in the dollar after the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its main interest rate on hold for a sixth month.\par \par \uc2 As the euro rose against the dollar on the ECB decision and a strong Spanish bond auction, the Colombian peso strengthened to COP1,759 for a dollar, up 0.5% from Wednesday's close.\par \par \uc2 Record-setting foreign investment into Colombia's oil sector caused the peso to rise nearly 10% against the dollar last year, making it one of the best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world. It is 0.4% stronger so far in 2013 and analysts say that without heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  the peso could continue to rise.\par \par \uc2 Write to Dan Molinski at dan.molinski@dowjones.com [ 10-01-13 1411GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130110e91a000yq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
