\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  peso slumps on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 685 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 2012\par 01:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar purchases hit peso\par \par \uc2 * Brazil traders eye renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso gains 0.34 pct, Brazil real firms 0.14 pct\par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds comments)\par \par \uc2 By Nelson Bocanegra and Danielle Fonseca\par \par \uc2 BOGOTA/SAO PAULO, Oct 22 (Reuters) - Colombia's peso fell on Monday as the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars to stem recent gains while Brazil's real edged back toward a level that could trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso weakened by the most in more than two months, shedding 0.53 percent against the dollar, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $30.6 million in the local market.\par \par \uc2 "The Colombian peso was the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region with the biggest losses, due to these strong \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  since last week by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Diana Guiza, an analyst at brokerage Corredores Asociados.\par \par \uc2 Last week, \uc2 Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped up dollar purchases to an average of $35 million per day compared to a previous plan to buy $20 million a day.\par \par \uc2 Colombia, Brazil and Peru are trying to contain gains in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as easy money policies in the United States, Europe and Japan push investors to seek out gains in higher-yielding emerging market assets.\par \par \uc2 Stronger local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  hurt domestic manufacturers as they suffer from competition with cheaper imports while making less profit on their exports.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, the real was up 0.14 percent at 2.0244 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Investors expected the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to soon roll over some $3 billion in reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps that expire on Nov. 1.\par \par \uc2 The contracts, which mimic the purchase of dollars in the futures market, were sold by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early September to stop the real from strengthening past 2 per dollar - a level the bank has been defending since early July to support Brazilian exporters.\par \par \uc2 Traders expect the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or its government to take further measures if the real rises much more.\par \par \uc2 "We think that the dollar will remain around this level and within a narrow range," Joao Medeiros, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at brokerage Pioneer.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso rose on renewed hopes that Spain would request financial aid.\par \par \uc2 Mexican policymakers are not expected to step up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts anytime soon. Gains in the peso are helping curb a spike in inflation by cheapening imports.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained 0.34 percent after the outcome of Spain's regional elections was seen as a boost to Prime Minister Mariano Rajoy's austerity drive.\par \par \uc2 The results rekindled hopes Madrid would soon request a sovereign bailout, seen by investors as crucial to mitigate the region's debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso has been supported by signs of faster growth in its top trading partner, the United States, and data on Monday showed Mexican retail sales in August were stronger than expected.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso has been one of the top performing emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, but gains have flagged in recent weeks as investors cashed in on the strong run-up in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The peso has gained nearly 9 percent against the dollar this year.\par \par \uc2 Data from the \uc2 Commodity Futures Trading Commission\uc2  showed on Friday that the number of investors betting on a stronger peso dipped in the latest week of data, but still hovered near a record high.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso slipped 0.5 percent as prices for copper, the country's top export, hit a more than one-month low.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 2130 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                             daily %  year-to-\par                                      change     ate %\par                            Latest              change\par Brazil real                  2.0244      0.14     -7.70\par                                              \par Mexico peso                 12.8565      0.34      8.71\par                                              \par Argentina peso*              6.2600      0.80    -24.44\par                                              \par Chile peso                 477.0000     -0.50      8.87\par                                              \par Colombia peso            1,808.1000     -0.53      7.21\par                                              \par Peru sol                     2.5760      0.08      4.70\par                                              \par * Argentine peso's rate between                        \par brokerages                                     \par                                   