\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed On Spain Concerns\b0\par\par\uc2 By Prabha Natarajan   \par \uc2 488 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Oktober 2012\par 22:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  seesawed Tuesday as investor mood swung to caution on headlines about Spain's plans to seek financial assistance.\par \par \uc2 A report indicated that Spanish Prime Minister Mariano Rajoy indicated he wasn't considering seeking a credit line to support the debt-laden country. Investors expect Spain eventually will require the help but may delay it as long as it can or at least until its provincial elections in November.\par \par \uc2 This led to a choppy ride for emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar opened the day lower against the Mexican peso at MXN12.7705 but later rose to MXN12.8419, up 0.3% on the day.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also received a boost after strong CPI in the U.S. and the strongest level of U.S. homebuilders' confidence since June 2006 left investors with little doubt about the strength of the country's economic recovery. The momentum could bring in buyers and push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  toward MXN12.6550/12.6650, according to a trader at Standard Chartered.\par \par \uc2 Some investors are using these dips to go long the U.S. dollar, suggesting that in the coming months they expect the dollar to strengthen in line with the fortunes of the economy.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Hungarian forint and Czech koruna, though, managed to make sizable gains against both the euro and the dollar. Investors find these higher yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  attractive. The forint is up 0.43% at 277.84 per euro, according to CQG data. Market participants suggest that the euro will trade in a range between HUF277.50 and HUF282.59 in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Turkish lira close to new highs, and market participant are looking to buy at the dips ahead of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting on Thursday, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to cut overnight lending rates for the second time since February. Turkey, faced with slowing growth, is expected to resort to rate cuts like other emerging economies. The dollar fetches TRY1.8036, down 0.38% on the day.\par \par \uc2 The stronger buying pace in the morning prompted several central banks to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Peru and Indonesia.\par \par \uc2 The USD/IDR is trading at 9605, late afternoon New York time, after it dropped below 9600 earlier in the day following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's attempts to hold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in that range.\par \par \uc2 Peru and \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to regulate the pace of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements. The Peruvian sol is trading almost flat on the day at PEN2.582 per dollar, while the Colombia peso is also unchanged at 1798.8 per dollar, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 In credit markets, \uc2 Perusahaan Listrik Negara\uc2 , the state-owned electricity company of Indonesia, sold $1 billion of 30-year notes at a yield of 5.35%. The deal tightened from its initial price.\par \par \uc2 Write to Prabha Natarajan at prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com [ 16-10-12 2035GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121016e8ag000y1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
