\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia Central Bank \highlight\uc2  September  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  Was $540 Million\b0\par\par\uc2 By Darcy Crowe   \par \uc2 171 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2012\par 22:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA--The \uc2 Colombian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Monday it had purchased $540 million in the spot market in September under its policy of buying dollars, part of its effort to curb the peso's strength and build up international reserves.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar purchases in the spot market are aimed at preventing excessive strength in the peso. The bank has bought $3.38 billion this year and has pledged to continue the daily purchases at least through March.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  used a similar strategy in 2011, when it purchased $3.72 billion.\par \par \uc2 Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after its monthly policy meeting in September, said its yearlong dollar-buying program in the spot market would continue for at least six more months.\par \par \uc2 The bank said it would buy "at least" $3 billion from October through March, and the daily minimum would be $20 million.\par \par \uc2 Write to Darcy Crowe at darcy.crowe@dowjones.com. [ 08-10-12 2043GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121008e8a8000zb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
